law.text:
		Adult services provided by the Department together with local departments of social services shall include:

Home-based services, including homemaker, companion, or chore services, which will allow individuals to attain or maintain self-care and are likely to prevent or reduce dependency, to the extent that federal or state matching funds are made available for such purpose;


Adult foster care, including recruitment, approval, and supervision of adult foster care homes;


Participation in nursing home pre-admission screenings of all individuals pursuant to § 32.1-330;


Provision of assisted living facility assessments of residents and applicants pursuant to § 63.2-1804;


Participation in long-term care service coordination pursuant to § 51.5-138;


Provision of social services or public assistance as defined in § 63.2-100, as appropriate, to consumers discharged from state hospitals or training centers pursuant to §§ 37.2-505 and 37.2-837; and


Participation in such other services or programs as may be required pursuant to state or federal law.
